---
import type { Tone } from './directions';
interface Props { header: Tone; body: Tone; band: Tone }
const { header, body, band } = Astro.props;
---

<section data-tone={header} class="border-b border-(--border)">
	<div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 pt-20 pb-14">
		<p class="font-mono text-xs tracking-wider text-(--accent) uppercase">About</p>
		<h1 class="mt-3 max-w-3xl text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-(--heading) sm:text-5xl">A club for students who want to understand markets, not just watch them.</h1>
		<p class="mt-5 max-w-2xl text-lg text-(--muted)">Boiler Quant was founded in 2019 by a handful of Purdue students who couldn't find a place on campus to talk about quantitative trading. Today we're one of the largest finance organizations at the university.</p>
	</div>
</section>

<section data-tone={body}>
	<div class="mx-auto grid max-w-6xl gap-12 px-6 py-16 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_280px]">
		<div class="demo-prose">
			<h2>Our mission</h2>
			<p>We exist to close the gap between what a university teaches and what a trading firm expects. Coursework gives you the mathematics; we give you the context, the tooling, and a group of people who will push you to apply it. Everything we do is hands-on: writing code, testing ideas against data, and being honest about what didn't work.</p>
			<p>Membership is open to every major and every year. Our most successful members have come from computer science, mathematics, statistics, electrical engineering, physics, and economics, and plenty of them had never written a line of trading code before they joined.</p>
			<blockquote>"The club gave me a reason to go deeper than the homework. By the time I interviewed, I'd already built the things they were asking about."</blockquote>
			<h2>How the semester works</h2>
			<p>Each semester opens with a callout and a short onboarding series covering market structure, probability, and our shared codebase. From there, members sort into project teams led by experienced members. Teams meet weekly and present their work at a final showcase that firms are invited to attend.</p>
			<ul>
				<li><strong>Weeks 1–3:</strong> Onboarding workshops and team formation.</li>
				<li><strong>Weeks 4–12:</strong> Project work, guest speakers, and trading competitions.</li>
				<li><strong>Weeks 13–15:</strong> Final presentations and the Chicago firm trek.</li>
			</ul>
			<h2>Partnering with us</h2>
			<p>Firms work with us to host speaker events, run workshops, sponsor competitions, and meet students before recruiting season. If you'd like to talk, <a href="#">email the exec board</a> and we'll get back to you within a few days.</p>
		</div>
		<aside class="space-y-4 self-start lg:sticky lg:top-24">
			<div class="rounded-lg border border-(--border) bg-(--card) p-5">
				<p class="font-mono text-xs tracking-wider text-(--accent) uppercase">At a glance</p>
				<dl class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-sm">
					{[['Founded', '2019'], ['Members', '120+'], ['Meetings', 'Weekly, Thu 6pm'], ['Location', 'Lawson 1142']].map(([k, v]) => (
						<div class="flex justify-between gap-4"><dt class="text-(--muted)">{k}</dt><dd class="font-mono">{v}</dd></div>
					))}
				</dl>
			</div>
			<a href="#" class="block rounded-md bg-(--btn-bg) px-5 py-3 text-center text-sm font-medium text-(--btn-fg) hover:bg-(--btn-hover)">Join the mailing list</a>
		</aside>
	</div>
</section>

<section data-tone={band} class="border-t border-(--border)">
	<div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 py-16">
		<h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-(--heading)">Where our members go</h2>
		<p class="mt-2 max-w-xl text-(--muted)">A sample of the firms where Boiler Quant alumni have interned or work full-time.</p>
		<div class="mt-8 grid grid-cols-2 gap-3 sm:grid-cols-3 lg:grid-cols-6">
			{['sig', 'optiver', 'imc', 'jump', 'akuna', 'point72', 'cme', 'citsec', 'goldmansachs', 'google', 'databricks', 'nvidia'].map((f) => (
				<div class="flex h-20 items-center justify-center rounded-md border border-(--border) bg-(--white) p-4">
					<img src={`/company_logos/${f}${f === 'citsec' ? '.jpg' : '.png'}`} alt={f} class="max-h-10 max-w-full object-contain" />
				</div>
			))}
		</div>
	</div>
</section>
